flowchart TB
  R[Researcher] --> C[Research Contract\nMarkdown: purpose • scope • authorization • acceptance]
  C --> E[Experiment Requirements\nYAML: workload • OS • isolation • network • instrumentation]
  E --> A[Primary Agent / Goose\nplan • select • provision • execute • observe • adapt]
  A -->|resolve| REG[Capability Registry\nversioned profiles]
  REG --> HP[Host Profile\nLinux + Lima/QEMU capabilities]
  REG --> WP[Workload Profile\nfixed handler + fixture]
  A -->|request capability| CAP[Go Capability API\nresolve • provision • execute • collect • destroy]
  CAP -->|policy gate| PC[policyctl\nvalidate • check • require • audit]
  PC -->|allow / approved| CAP
  PC -->|deny| STOP[STOP]
  CAP --> VM[Lima / QEMU Disposable VM\nexecution + isolation boundary]
  HP --> CAP
  WP --> CAP
  CAP --> INST[Declared Instrumentation\nprocess • syscall • filesystem • network]
  INST --> VM
  VM --> WORK[Workload Handler\nGo • npm • controlled fixtures]
  WORK --> EV[Evidence Bundle\nraw observations + audit events]
  EV --> HASH[Session / Provenance\nSHA-256 + manifest]
  HASH --> ANALYZE[Specialist Roles + Skills\nruntime • forensics • detection]
  ANALYZE --> VERIFY[Independent Verifier]
  VERIFY --> REPORT[Research Report]
  REPORT --> PRESERVE[Preserve artifacts]
  PRESERVE --> DESTROY[Destroy VM]
  DESTROY --> A
  EXT[Pluggable Providers\nLima • future QEMU/WSL2/container] -.-> CAP
  SK[Skills / MCP / Gateways / Observability] -.-> A
